drm/msm: Shut down the GPU hangcheck timer before freeing rings

The timer callback dereferences the active ring and can rearm itself.
Synchronously stop it before destroying any rings. A valid worker means
msm_gpu_init() reached timer_setup(): there are no failures between the
two initialization steps.

This closes the timer producer at final cleanup. It does not fence IRQ
or IOMMU producers, drain recovery before the GMU component unbind, or
stop in-flight DMA after a suspend timeout.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -1043,6 +1043,10 @@ void msm_gpu_cleanup(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 
 	DBG("%s", gpu->name);
 
+	/* hangcheck_handler() reads the rings and may rearm the timer. */
+	if (gpu->worker)
+		timer_shutdown_sync(&gpu->hangcheck_timer);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(gpu->rb); i++) {
 		msm_ringbuffer_destroy(gpu->rb[i]);
 		gpu->rb[i] = NULL;
